As well as these forecasts, Fugro has a buoy based near to the client which produces hourly observations of the sea state. Data assimilation refers to a range of techniques used to integrate observations into a forecast, with the aim of making the forecast more accurate. In this project, we explore the potential of DA to reduce uncertainty and error in these wave forecasts. We hope that DA will give better results than the alpha factor method currently in use.

